.TH DLOCKHISTORY 8 "2026-10-26"
.SH NAME
dlockhistory \- keep the Diablo history hash table locked in memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dlockhistory
[
.B \-a
]
[
.B \-f
]
[
.B \-s
.I sleeptime
]
[
.B \-V
]
.I historyfile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dlockhistory
maps the hash table of a history file (normally /news/dhistory) and locks
it into memory with
.IR mlock (2),
so that history lookups don't wait for the disk.  It keeps running and
checks every 5 seconds (\-s) whether the history file was replaced (a new inode,
for example after
.IR dhisexpire (8)),
and then maps and locks the new file.
.PP
.IR mlock (2)
usually needs root, so
.I dlockhistory
refuses to run as another user unless
.B \-f
is given.  Running it as root is a risk; make sure you need it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Lock the whole history file, not only the hash table.
.TP
.B \-f
Don't check for root.
.TP
.BI \-s " sleeptime"
Check for a new history file every sleeptime seconds (default 5).
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diablo(8),
dhisexpire(8),
dilookup(8)
